1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:29,860
Let's have Coach Tony give us a song! Sound good?

3
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,700
I was riding my bike and playing video games,

4
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,540
specifically picking activities that burn the most energy.

5
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:37,980
My mom's not sick.

6
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:39,420
But Chuck said

7
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:41,340
I could use that as an excuse to skip Practice.

8
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,780
I'm just really worried I'm not gonna grow tall enough.

9
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,140
So... I decided to go home and sleep more.

10
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,600
So what?

11
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,500
Do you all think you're so amazing?

12
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:50,460
Matthew!

13
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:52,860
Whoa, no need to shout.

14
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:54,780
So unladylike.

15
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:00,000
Episode 25

16
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:03,900
Too bad I don't see any "true gentleman"
standing in front of me.

17
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:06,150
Zoe, I was only cutting you some slack

18
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,260
because you're a girl.

19
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:10,140
But since you're pushing it,

20
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,580
you've asked for it.

21
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,460
I don't need you to cut me any slack.

22
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,340
Fine, have it your way.

23
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,260
I'll show you what the Jianghai Team is made of!

24
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,660
Hmph. The Chengnan Team doesn't scare that easily.

25
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,200
Let's go.

26
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,500
Bring it on. Let's go.

27
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,340
Could you guys just cut me some slack here?

28
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,220
Power Vortex!

29
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:21,660
Heavenly Fiend Whirlwind!

30
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Would you look at that?

31
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:44,700
The Jianghai Team's just all hype and no bite.

32
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:48,540
Today was just a warning.
Don't underestimate the Chengnan Team from now on.

33
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:50,940
Hmph. I'm not in the mood today.

34
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:52,860
Matthew, we'll chat another time.

35
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:53,980
Chat? Again?

36
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,200
Of course.

37
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,220
See ya.

38
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:04,380
Oh, heavens above!

39
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:08,220
A guy like me, Teddy, actually lost to Zoe.

40
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:13,020
If word of this gets out,
how am I supposed to show my face in public?

41
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,380
Alright, alright. I won't tell a soul.

42
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:20,700
You're a real pal.

43
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,260
I just can't get the hang of this Crimson Holy Light.

44
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,660
Maybe this whole idea is just a dead end?

45
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,100
No way.

46
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:49,500
The problem is Fire Warrior

47
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:52,380
just doesn't have what it takes to
Master the Ultimate Holy Light yet.

48
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:55,740
So should I try upgrading my Fire Warrior

49
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,660
to the Blazing Light Wave first?

50
00:05:58,300 --> 00:05:59,580
Not quite.

51
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,950
Upgrading the Fire Warrior

52
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:03,420
needs to be guided by the right moves.

53
00:06:07,320 --> 00:06:09,660
So I still gotta Master the Blue Holy Light first, huh?

54
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:12,060
That's the theory, anyway.

55
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,420
Guess I'll just keep practicing then.

56
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:20,220
But trying to pull it off with just the
Fire Warrior is gonna be tough.

57
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:22,620
So which move should I even be practicing?

58
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,060
I'm totally lost here.

59
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:26,940
Honestly? I'm not really sure either.

60
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,820
Whoa, so even you don't know everything?

61
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:32,220
What, you think I'm some kind of wizard?

62
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:34,620
I actually thought you were.

63
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,540
So I guess the problem you're having

64
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,940
is beyond even a wizard's help.

65
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,820
Alright, I'm out. Gonna go catch some sleep.

66
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,940
Fine! Then I'll just take on this wizard myself!

67
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:55,740
No way! You're kidding, right?

68
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,960
You're kidding, right?

69
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:01,980
Shawn, stop messing around.

70
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,860
Zoe couldn't even beat Popcorn last time!

71
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:07,740
I swear it's true! I saw the whole thing with my own eyes.

72
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,140
That's even crazier than a Chinese Novel.

73
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:13,980
I'm telling you, that Teddy must be under some kind of spell.

74
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:17,340
No, It's not a spell. He's been played.

75
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:19,000
I'm telling you,

76
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:22,620
Teddy totally fell for Zoe's honey trap.

77
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:24,060
What are you talking about?

78
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:26,460
That's Zoe we are talking about.

79
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,820
What "honey trap"?

80
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,220
If anyone was gonna fall for a honey trap, it wouldn't be Teddy.

81
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,620
It'd be Matthew!

82
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:37,500
I just got word.

83
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,350
The Chengnan Team is already gearing up
and eyeing us like a hawk.

84
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,300
They're completely prepared.

85
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:45,150
And here's the proof.

86
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:47,580
The Chengnan Team practices twice a week.

87
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,020
That's one more time than us.

88
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,460
Which means

89
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:53,340
they've got double the preparation time we do.

90
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:55,230
Double the time means,

91
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:58,140
double the chance to build up their Individual Skills,

92
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:59,200
Stop!

93
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,980
and sharpen their instincts.

94
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:07,260
Our hero has arrived!

95
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:11,100
Teddy, what's going on?

96
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,460
I really didn't say anything.

97
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,860
So I lost to Zoe. Big deal.

98
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:20,220
Like the old saying goes:
"even the best have an off day."

99
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,140
This is not some minor thing!

100
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:23,580
Well, what do you want me to do?

101
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,020
I already lost.

102
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,940
Victory and defeat are all part of the game.

103
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:29,340
Stop making excuses.

104
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:32,220
Mark, I think losing 1 match might actually be a good thing.

105
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:33,180
At the very least,

106
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,100
it'll remind everyone

107
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:38,460
not to get complacent from now on.

108
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:40,380
Right now, our top priority is to train harder.

109
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,750
Otherwise, we're falling behind.

110
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:44,700
Yeah. I propose we increase the number
of Weekly Training Sessions.

111
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:47,100
What does everyone think?

112
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,540
No problem.

113
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,130
Oh no... this is it. We're done for.

114
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:50,940
This is the end.

115
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:51,900
What's wrong?

116
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,820
Monica, what happened?

117
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,190
I... I don't dare say it.

118
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,660
If I tell you, you won't be able to handle it.

119
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:00,060
Women. Just can't handle a little turbulence.

120
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:02,460
So what if Teddy lost. What's the big deal?

121
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:04,350
Wait, Teddy lost?

122
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:05,340
That's not why I'm upset!

123
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,000
This is "Explosive News!"

124
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,000
Tell us!

125
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:10,620
Just let me have some water first.

126
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,860
From the intense Energy I'm picking up right now,

127
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:21,660
this is no small matter.

128
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:24,060
You guys better brace yourselves.

129
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,460
We're already braced! Just spit it out!

130
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:27,900
Are you gonna tell us or not?

131
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:29,340
Just let me have 1 more sip.

132
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:33,150
If you're not gonna spill,
we're not listening. Let's go practice.

133
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,100
Alright, alright! Listen!

134
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:36,920
There might be some of us who
can't compete in the Tournament!

135
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:37,960
What?

136
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:43,260
How could that be?

137
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:46,000
I'm sure I saw him.

138
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:47,580
I saw Coach Tony standing right here.

139
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:49,500
And Principal Qian was standing right there.

140
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,380
With my own ears I heard Principal Qian say

141
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:54,300
that the School just got a Notification.

142
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,670
The Team Event for the Autumn Yo-Yo Tournament

143
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,620
is cutting its roster down to 6 people.

144
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:02,030
That means 2 of our Players are gonna have to drop out.

145
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,820
Popcorn, are you hallucinating or something?

146
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:08,700
Maybe you just didn't hear the whole conversation.

147
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,140
Everyone, just stop.

148
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:13,020
We'll know for sure once Coach Tony gets back.

149
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:14,940
What if Coach Tony doesn't come back?

150
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:17,150
Why wouldn't he?

151
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:19,140
Because he's scared to face us.

152
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,630
You think Coach Tony is like you or something?

153
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:22,800
If this news is actually true,

154
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:24,060
I think...

155
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:26,940
Coach Tony is gonna be even more
upset about it than we are.

156
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:30,300
No matter what, we're still gonna Compete.

157
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:34,140
Let's head back to the training hall first.

158
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:45,180
My horoscope said I'd hit a major setback this week.

159
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:56,220
Chaos. The Energy in here is totally chaotic.

160
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:00,990
Hey, Shawn! Stop scurrying around everywhere.

161
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,460
Even if you were an actual Squirrel,

162
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,830
you should take a break.

163
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,780
I'm trying to come up with a strategy here!

164
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:09,540
Alright, alright. Besides "strategies,"
what else have you got?

165
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,000
Why are you snapping at me?

166
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,740
Sis, let me put some lubricant on that for you.

167
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:20,700
Mm.

168
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:33,660
Leo, what do you think?

169
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:37,980
If that's really the case, I think I have a plan.

170
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:42,780
Coach!

171
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:47,580
Coach, is this really happening?

172
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:50,460
Coach, isn't there any way we can fight this?

173
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,780
Everyone.

174
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:58,140
I just got off the phone with the Tournament Organizers.

175
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,060
Within this week,

176
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:04,380
we need to select 6 Members for our Official Roster.

177
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:07,260
And then we'll submit the list.

178
00:12:08,300 --> 00:12:10,280
Sigh, take care.

179
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,500
Hey, why are you pretending like I'm
the one getting cut from the Team.

180
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,870
Who said you were getting cut?

181
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:16,860
Then why'd you pat me on the back?

182
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,260
Well, you were standing closest to me.

183
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,660
What's all the yelling? Stop being so paranoid.

184
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,060
So who's actually getting cut?

185
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:25,520
Well, I'm not getting cut, that's for sure.

186
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
And neither am I.

187
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,260
I'm not leaving either.

188
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:30,780
Quiet, everyone. Let's hear what Coach Tony has to say.

189
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,070
Leo.

190
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:37,980
You're the Captain. What do you think we should do?

191
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,900
I've already talked it over with Mark.

192
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,820
It seems like there's only one way.

193
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:44,700
In 2 days, we'll hold a Full-Team Skill Competition.

194
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:47,100
A Competition? Isn't that a little harsh?

195
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:48,540
I'm all for it.

196
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:52,380
Sometimes a single Competition doesn't
really show your true Skill.

197
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:54,780
Well, what else do you suggest we do?

198
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:00,060
Does anyone have any other suggestions?

199
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:03,420
I guess this is the only way.

200
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:04,380
Alright.

201
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,780
Then that's settled.

202
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:09,660
I know.

203
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:12,540
You've all poured a ton of sweat and hard work

204
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,460
into bringing honor to the Jianghai Team.

205
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:18,780
But reality is often this harsh.

206
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:23,100
But, we can't let this break our spirit.

207
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:24,510
Our goal

208
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:26,460
is to select the absolute best Players

209
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,500
to represent the Jianghai Team.

210
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:31,500
So when you all get home,

211
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:32,700
use your time to practice hard.

212
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:35,100
Get ready for the Full-Team Competition in 2 days.

213
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:37,980
Are you ready for this?

214
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:38,980
Yeah!

215
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:59,550
Slide up, slide down. Catch and release.

216
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,900
Back and forth, the styles shift and change endlessly.

217
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,300
It's really not that simple.

218
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:12,060
A timeless sport, filled with wisdom and purpose.

219
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,420
Between the rise and fall, speed and power work together.

220
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:17,820
A workout for both body and mind.

221
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:23,580
Soaring high and dipping low, an eternal law of motion.

222
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:29,340
Spinning 'round and 'round without end,
igniting the spark of life itself.

223
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:35,100
A blazing fire burns inside my heart,
incinerating all confusion.

224
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:38,940
This raging heat becomes my strength,
forging me like tempered steel.

225
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:40,860
It must be honed and polished.

226
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:47,100
A blazing fire burns inside my heart,
shattering all fear and breaking every barrier.

227
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:50,430
Strive constantly to grow and break on through.

228
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:56,300
These youthful years belong to me to seize and take control.

229
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:13,980
The Yo-Yo spins, the joy it brings is truly infinite.

230
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:16,860
Facing every challenge, overcoming each and every trial.

231
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:19,740
I'm ready for the test.

232
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:25,020
My unwavering faith will never, ever change.

233
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,860
Without a real contest, without the sting of failure,

234
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:31,230
how can you ever move forward?

